# Empty on purpose: in production the app is served by the Cloudflare
# Worker (see worker/index.ts + wrangler.jsonc), which proxies /api/* to the
# Django backend on the same origin the browser sees. An empty value here
# makes authApi.ts's `API_BASE_URL` resolve to "" (same origin) instead of
# the local dev default in .env.example — that's what lets the httpOnly
# refresh-token cookie (SameSite=Lax) be sent at all.
#
# IMPORTANT: if the Cloudflare project has a VITE_API_BASE_URL environment
# variable configured in its dashboard build settings, that value wins over
# this file (Vite gives real process.env vars priority over committed .env
# files) — it needs to be removed or emptied there too, or the production
# build will keep calling the Render URL directly and this migration won't
# take effect.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
